# /etc/cron.d/antweb-place-daily -- antweb-prod (ssh root@165.232.137.86). Installed by hand, never by a deploy:
# see docs/runbook.md, "Places from coordinates". Remove: rm /etc/cron.d/antweb-place-daily
#
# Every day 09:10 Pacific, after the daily update (05:00, done by about 08:00): tools/place/place_daily.py, report
# mode. What the coordinates say each specimen's country and state should be goes into the table place_update; the
# specimens are not changed (Brian 2026-11-16: one week of reports first). Log: journalctl -t place-daily
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MAILTO=""
10 9 * * * root /usr/bin/python3 /root/antweb/tools/place/place_daily.py >/dev/null 2>&1
